{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\ntest_cli_show_complete_or_erroring_under_write_burst costs 10.95-22.63s in recent CI samples and is the largest variable default-suite node. Closed slim-fetch-ledge is the original regression and must remain protected. Closed ambery-enigmatic-pussycat later added a generic table-driven reads-under-writer-storm property but intentionally retained the original show regression byte-for-byte. Runtime overlap alone does not prove redundancy.\n\n## Plan\n- Map both tests through the CLI, store read/reconvergence, writer process, output-completeness, exit-code, timeout, and cleanup paths.\n- Enumerate the original slim-fetch-ledge failure mechanism and any failure classes only the generic property reaches.\n- Seed each defect independently and run both oracles to establish a detection matrix.\n- If the generic property misses any original behavior, keep both or strengthen it under legitimate RED-to-GREEN before considering consolidation.\n- Measure repeated macOS and Ubuntu timings and compare concurrency-regression practice in maintained OSS projects.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- Run `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py` with each fault seed applied independently and record the expected RED detection matrix.\n- Restore production behavior and run the same focused command GREEN, including its real subprocess timeout and cleanup assertions.\n- Run the repository gates with `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The original empty-or-partial-success regression remains detectable through the real CLI.\n- [x] Fault-seeded evidence identifies which oracle detects every original failure class.\n- [x] Fault-seeded evidence identifies which oracle detects every generic failure class.\n- [x] Process concurrency remains real.\n- [x] Output completeness remains observable.\n- [x] Exit status remains observable.\n- [x] Timeout enforcement remains observable.\n- [x] Process cleanup remains observable.\n- [x] Any consolidation removes an oracle only after behavioral equivalence is proven.\n- [x] Repeated macOS wall-clock timings are recorded.\n- [x] Repeated Ubuntu wall-clock timings are recorded.\n- [x] Aggregate runner savings are calculated from the measured samples.\n- [x] The resulting evidence cites slim-fetch-ledge and ambery-enigmatic-pussycat.\n- [x] The resulting evidence cites maintained OSS concurrency-regression precedents."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787173753852098001,"uuid":"c222af12-eb42-493f-acc2-ab2465b14ad3"}